{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### What was wrong\n\n`median` had the even-length case inverted: the docstring says to average the two middle values, but the code returned `s[mid - 1]` only (for `[1, 2, 3, 4]` that gave `2` instead of `2.5`). Odd-length behavior was already correct.\n\n### What changed\n\n- **Even `n`:** `(s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2`\n- **Odd `n`:** unchanged (`s[mid]`)\n- Removed the inline bug note and used a straightforward `if n % 2` branch instead of a confusing ternary\n- Left `old_median` as a thin alias for v1 dashboards (nothing else in the repo imports it)\n\nBoth tests in `tests/visible/test_stats.py` pass. `stats_summary` in `repo/rows.py` will now report the correct median for even-sized columns."}]},"session_id":"b69d42fd-5c06-4220-9e84-088e154ac0cc"}
